The total circumference is the sum of the circumferences of all four circles:

\[
C_{\text{total}} = 2\pi(5\,\text{cm}) + 2\pi(10\,\text{cm}) + 2\pi(15\,\text{cm}) + 2\pi(20\,\text{cm})
                 = 2\pi(5+10+15+20)\,\text{cm}
                 = 2\pi(50)\,\text{cm}
                 = 100\pi\,\text{cm}
\]

So the total circumference is **\(100\pi\) cm**, which is approximately **314.16 cm**.
